{
  "name": "claudeconnect",
  "version": "2.5.3",
  "released": "2026-10-14",
  "notes": [
    "Signing in to claude.ai during setup works on a Mac now. The install command handed setup your terminal as /dev/tty, which Claude Code can't read the keyboard from on a Mac, so its sign-in crashed with \"EINVAL: invalid argument, kqueue\" (2.5.2 didn't fix the cause). The install command now hands over your terminal by its own name.",
    "A site that's already running was never affected: it talks to Claude Code another way, not through the terminal."
  ],
